{
  "teamId": 137,
  "year": 2026,
  "narrative": "The 2026 San Francisco Giants were a team that never found its footing, stumbling through a season defined by pitching collapses, untimely errors, and flashes of offensive promise that arrived too late to matter. From the very first week of meaningful action in late April, the bullpen and rotation alike were hemorrhaging runs, turning competitive games into blowouts and dashing any early optimism that this roster might surprise the National League West.\n\nThe month of May encapsulated everything wrong with this Giants squad. Ryan Walker, Matt Gage, and Caleb Kilian were repeatedly burned for multi-run hits at the worst possible moments, with Ketel Marte's devastating three-run homer off Gage on May 19th standing as the season's single most damaging blow to that point. Even the rare defensive gem — Nolan Arenado grounding into a double play that briefly saved Kilian — felt like a borrowed moment of grace in an otherwise grim spring.\n\nJune offered the season's most tantalizing glimpse of what might have been. Bryce Eldridge's grand slam, Rafael Devers launching a go-ahead shot, Victor Bericoto's emerging power, and Jung Hoo Lee's clutch triple gave Oracle Park something to cheer about. Willy Adames contributed throughout as a steadying offensive presence, and for a few weeks the Giants played baseball that resembled a legitimate contender. But the rotation could never sustain the momentum, and by July the wheels came off again as Dylan Smith and Logan Webb were carved up by opposing lineups.\n\nThe second half was a slow, painful march toward elimination. Dylan Smith surrendered pivotal hits in back-to-back August outings, Carson Seymour was torched for a three-run homer by Bo Bichette in September, and a costly throwing error by Osleivis Basabe typified the sloppy, dispirited play that had become the Giants' signature. A 65-97 record told the story plainly: this was one of San Francisco's worst seasons in recent memory, a rebuilding year that exposed the distance still remaining between this roster and playoff contention.",
